# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
!web/dist/
!web/dist/**
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Node (web/) — not part of the original 3-line dist/ patch (WEB_DESIGN.md §0.1-A) or its
# owner's own edits, but its absence is a real gap: without it `npm install`/`npm ci` in web/
# leaves ~300 packages' worth of files untracked, one `git add -A` away from committing the
# entire dependency tree. `web/package-lock.json` is what CI restores from; `node_modules/`
# itself never belongs in git regardless of which subdirectory it grows in.
node_modules/

# Local databases and ingest artifacts
*.db
*.db-journal
# SQLite's write-ahead-log sidecars. `*.db` does not match `hardwood.db-wal`, so the first
# `web.sh dev` used to leave two untracked files with cryptic names in `git status`.
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
/data/
backend/hardwood.db

# Real EuroLeague and injury-report data never enters git (EUROLEAGUE_DESIGN §0.6; the "Repository
# hygiene" note at the end of docs/LEGAL.md §2e). This repository is public. Recorded API responses,
# NBA injury-report PDFs and the user's workbook live under $HARDWOOD_DATA_DIR on the machine that
# made them, or in backend/tests/local/, whose *contents* are ignored. The design names the
# directory itself; ignoring only its contents lets the few files that must be committed stay
# committable (the replay test, which reads the real workbook at run time and holds none of it,
# and the .gitkeep that keeps nba_injury/ in a fresh clone). Git cannot re-include a file whose
# parent directory is excluded, hence the four-line pattern:
#   1 ignore everything directly under local/        3 look inside its sub-directories
#   2 except Python files (test modules)             4 but ignore what is in them, except .gitkeep
backend/tests/local/*
!backend/tests/local/*.py
!backend/tests/local/*/
backend/tests/local/*/*
!backend/tests/local/*/.gitkeep
# Probe output (euroleague probe, probe_nba_injury_report) and the gzipped raw payload store, wherever
# a data directory happens to sit.
**/recordings/
**/el-raw/
# The user's workbook is real data (and a gambling tool's output). It is read from the inbox or from
# HARDWOOD_WORKBOOK_PATH; no test fixture is a workbook, they are built in memory.
*.xlsx
*.xlsm

# Hardwood Web secrets and local-only account state (WEB_DESIGN.md §0.1-A, §2.1, §4.6)
backend/.env
*.p8
.hardwood-mail/

# Xcode
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
DerivedData/
*.xcscmblueprint
*.xccheckout
.swiftpm/

# macOS
.DS_Store
